{"audio":{"src":"https://pub-13abeb101e2945d2a7f60234f6faf52e.r2.dev/materials/a1-grammar-build-a-sentence/audio/main-598c55c36f07.mp3","durationSec":209.496,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":1.48,"text":"Emma and Ben are in class."},{"start":1.48,"end":3.38,"text":"Be means am, is or are."},{"start":3.64,"end":5.94,"text":"It tells who, how old, where or how someone is."},{"start":6.32,"end":7.94,"text":"Person, Be, Short form."},{"start":8.54,"end":9.48,"text":"I, am, I'm."},{"start":9.8,"end":11.72,"text":"he, she, it, is, he's, she's, it's."},{"start":12.04,"end":14.3,"text":"you, we, they, are, you're, we're, they're."},{"start":14.3,"end":16.62,"text":"Rule: Match am, is or are to the person."},{"start":17.16,"end":17.64,"text":"I am Ben."},{"start":17.86,"end":18.44,"text":"I'm at school."},{"start":18.78,"end":19.26,"text":"Is Emma ready?"},{"start":19.72,"end":20.38,"text":"Yes, she is."},{"start":20.72,"end":21.4,"text":"/ No, she isn't."},{"start":21.52,"end":22.04,"text":"(Emma = she)."},{"start":22.34,"end":22.76,"text":"Are you happy?"},{"start":23.3,"end":24.12,"text":"Yes, I am."},{"start":24.44,"end":25.26,"text":"/ No, I'm not."},{"start":25.72,"end":26.4,"text":"Ben is not tired."},{"start":26.56,"end":27.16,"text":"He isn't tired."},{"start":27.56,"end":28.02,"text":"(Ben = he)."},{"start":28.5,"end":29.22,"text":"We are at school."},{"start":29.22,"end":30.3,"text":"They are at home."},{"start":30.8,"end":32.64,"text":"Watch out:\n\nWrong: She are ready."},{"start":33.1,"end":34.26,"text":"Right: She is ready."},{"start":34.96,"end":36.22,"text":"Use is with he, she and it."},{"start":36.76,"end":37.16,"text":"Are you happy?"},{"start":37.54,"end":38.72,"text":"Wrong: Yes, you are."},{"start":39.08,"end":40.38,"text":"Right: Yes, I am."},{"start":40.38,"end":42.24,"text":"Answer about yourself with I."},{"start":42.76,"end":45.62,"text":"Answer about your group with we: Yes, we are."},{"start":46.58,"end":47.72,"text":"Emma and Ben talk in class."},{"start":48.12,"end":49.12,"text":"English words go in order."},{"start":49.42,"end":51.8,"text":"The verb is be or a doing word, like read."},{"start":52.38,"end":53.94,"text":"Person, Verb, More words."},{"start":54.48,"end":55.42,"text":"Ben, is, happy."},{"start":56,"end":57.62,"text":"We, read, books."},{"start":57.94,"end":63.46,"text":"In a question, be comes first:\n\nBe, Person, More words."},{"start":63.46,"end":66.94,"text":"Is, Ben, happy."},{"start":67.8,"end":70.72,"text":"Are, they, at school."},{"start":71.88,"end":76.38,"text":"Rule: The person comes first, then the verb."},{"start":76.92,"end":79.22,"text":"In a question, be comes before the person."},{"start":79.8,"end":82.16,"text":"Where comes first, then is or are, then the person."},{"start":82.88,"end":83.66,"text":"Ben is happy."},{"start":84.04,"end":84.4,"text":"We read."},{"start":84.92,"end":86.06,"text":"This short sentence is OK."},{"start":86.06,"end":88.2,"text":"They play games after school."},{"start":88.52,"end":89.1,"text":"Is Ben happy?"},{"start":89.78,"end":90.74,"text":"Yes, he is."},{"start":91,"end":92.16,"text":"/ No, he isn't."},{"start":92.68,"end":93.54,"text":"They are not at school."},{"start":94.14,"end":94.5,"text":"Where is Emma?"},{"start":94.96,"end":95.74,"text":"She is in the park."},{"start":96.54,"end":98.42,"text":"Watch out:\n\nWrong: Happy is Ben."},{"start":98.88,"end":100.16,"text":"Right: Ben is happy."},{"start":100.68,"end":101.64,"text":"The person comes first."},{"start":102.24,"end":103.1,"text":"Wrong: Do you are ready?"},{"start":103.64,"end":104.5,"text":"Right: Are you ready?"},{"start":105.36,"end":107.78,"text":"Never use do with am, is or are."},{"start":108.18,"end":109.76,"text":"Study: Look at these sentences."},{"start":110.34,"end":110.76,"text":"What moves?"},{"start":111.34,"end":112.12,"text":"Emma is at school."},{"start":112.76,"end":113.5,"text":"Is Emma at school?"},{"start":114,"end":114.66,"text":"Ben is at the door."},{"start":115.05,"end":119.02,"text":"Be tells who, how old, where or how someone is."},{"start":119.42,"end":122.34,"text":"An action verb is a doing word, like walk, eat or play."},{"start":123,"end":124.06,"text":"Be, Doing word."},{"start":124.06,"end":126.08,"text":"I am tired, I eat lunch."},{"start":126.68,"end":128.32,"text":"We are at school, We walk to school."},{"start":128.9,"end":130.42,"text":"They are happy, They play games."},{"start":131.06,"end":133.34,"text":"Rule: Use be or a doing word, not both."},{"start":133.98,"end":134.54,"text":"I am tired."},{"start":134.9,"end":135.54,"text":"I go to bed."},{"start":136,"end":136.74,"text":"Is Ben at the door?"},{"start":137.48,"end":138.24,"text":"Yes, he is."},{"start":139.02,"end":140.62,"text":"/ No, he isn't."},{"start":142.16,"end":143.68,"text":"Emma and Ben aren't tired."},{"start":144.12,"end":144.96,"text":"They play games."},{"start":145.5,"end":146.7,"text":"They read books after school."},{"start":147.94,"end":150.68,"text":"Watch out:\n\nWrong: I am go to school."},{"start":151.64,"end":153.28,"text":"Right: I go to school."},{"start":153.78,"end":154.6,"text":"Go is the doing word."},{"start":155.08,"end":155.64,"text":"Am is extra."},{"start":156.24,"end":157.28,"text":"Wrong: She happy."},{"start":157.86,"end":159,"text":"Right: She is happy."},{"start":159.38,"end":160.52,"text":"Happy is not a doing word."},{"start":161.22,"end":162.46,"text":"Our teacher writes on the board."},{"start":163.04,"end":165.48,"text":"A capital letter is a big letter, like A or B."},{"start":166.44,"end":168.54,"text":"Sentence, Ends with, Example."},{"start":169.42,"end":171.36,"text":"telling, full stop , Emma is here."},{"start":172.16,"end":174.5,"text":"asking, question mark , Is Emma here."},{"start":175.68,"end":177.24,"text":"Rule: Start with a capital letter."},{"start":177.52,"end":179.44,"text":"End with a full stop or a question mark."},{"start":179.84,"end":180.38,"text":"I am here."},{"start":180.9,"end":181.78,"text":"Emma and I are friends."},{"start":182.24,"end":182.74,"text":"Is Ben ready?"},{"start":183.3,"end":184,"text":"Yes, he is."},{"start":184.32,"end":184.9,"text":"They are not late."},{"start":185.76,"end":187.84,"text":"Watch out:\n\nWrong: are you ready."},{"start":188.38,"end":189.42,"text":"Right: Are you ready?"},{"start":189.86,"end":191.66,"text":"A question ends with a question mark."},{"start":192.34,"end":193.9,"text":"Wrong: ben and i play."},{"start":194.52,"end":195.84,"text":"Right: Ben and I play."},{"start":196.46,"end":197.76,"text":"Names and I need a capital letter."},{"start":198.14,"end":199.72,"text":"Wrong: Weareready."},{"start":199.72,"end":200.82,"text":"Right: We are ready."},{"start":201.32,"end":202.72,"text":"Put one space between words."},{"start":203.26,"end":205.68,"text":"Spelling:\n\nAlways write I as a capital letter."},{"start":206.42,"end":209.02,"text":"Names start with a capital letter: Emma, Ben."}],"words":[{"text":"Emma","start":0,"end":0.2},{"text":"and","start":0.2,"end":0.44},{"text":"Ben","start":0.44,"end":0.68},{"text":"are","start":0.68,"end":0.94},{"text":"in","start":0.94,"end":1.08},{"text":"class","start":1.08,"end":1.48},{"text":"Be","start":1.48,"end":2.02},{"text":"means","start":2.02,"end":2.4},{"text":"am","start":2.4,"end":2.7},{"text":"is","start":2.82,"end":2.96},{"text":"or","start":3,"end":3.12},{"text":"are","start":3.12,"end":3.38},{"text":"It","start":3.64,"end":3.72},{"text":"tells","start":3.72,"end":3.92},{"text":"who","start":3.92,"end":4.28},{"text":"how","start":4.32,"end":4.54},{"text":"old","start":4.54,"end":4.8},{"text":"where","start":4.88,"end":5.08},{"text":"or","start":5.16,"end":5.22},{"text":"how","start":5.22,"end":5.36},{"text":"someone","start":5.36,"end":5.64},{"text":"is","start":5.64,"end":5.94},{"text":"Person","start":6.32,"end":6.54},{"text":"Be","start":7.02,"end":7.12},{"text":"Short","start":7.26,"end":7.6},{"text":"form","start":7.6,"end":7.94},{"text":"I","s